From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: msi: Keep transform rows with NULL binary fields.

AI-assisted (Codex), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

Our Windows 10 x86_64/i686 MEASURE applies an original two-row transform
with a missing binary stream for its NULL-object row and a populated binary
control. Both rows, their notes and the control payload survive. Reading
the NULL field returns ERROR_INVALID_DATA with zero bytes. Wine dropped
the entire row when opening the absent stream failed.

v2 (2026-11-09): Keep the production implementation unchanged and add the
Windows-derived database test. Build the original transform via public
IStorage APIs rather than requiring Wine's unimplemented transform generator.
Check row retention, NULL/read semantics and the populated control with
ordinary ok() assertions. Native assertion L1, cross review and paired MSI
runtime remain pending. This does not establish the production workaround's
behavior for corrupt or inaccessible non-NULL streams. No series change.

diff --git a/dlls/msi/table.c b/dlls/msi/table.c
index 089f2027..cf04690a 100644
